Update Manager — installers
===========================

One-time setup per machine. Each installer creates a virtualenv in <app>/env and
installs the dependencies there, so the launchers (and the self-updater) find them.
Each script is labelled in its header with the OS it is dedicated to.

  linux/install.sh         Linux / Raspberry Pi. If a dependency (usually Pillow)
                           can't install from PyPI, it falls back to the prebuilt
                           Pillow from the system packages (needs sudo). It also adds
                           "Update Manager" to the applications menu.
                           Run:  chmod +x install.sh && ./install.sh   (or: bash install.sh)

  macos/install.command    macOS.  Run once: chmod +x install.command, then double-click.

  windows/install.ps1      Windows.
                           Run:  powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File install.ps1

Uninstallers (remove menu entries / Desktop shortcut, the env/ and caches; keep your
source, config.ini and secrets.ini):

  linux/uninstall.sh       bash install/linux/uninstall.sh
  macos/uninstall.command  bash install/macos/uninstall.command
  windows/uninstall.ps1    powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File install\windows\uninstall.ps1

After installing, launch from launchers/<os>/ (see launchers/README), from the Linux
applications menu, or run `python updatemanager.py` inside the activated env.

The env/ folder is gitignored and never committed.
